# Local credentials for `netlify dev`, so the Hub's own endpoints answer in the
# preview (2026-11-18). Copy to `.env` and fill in the two tokens.
#
# WHY THIS IS NEEDED AT ALL. The site has BLOBS_TOKEN and github_token set on
# Netlify, but both are marked SECRET, which means the CLI cannot read them
# back — only the deployed runtime sees them. `netlify dev` therefore injects
# BLOBS_SITE_ID and nothing else, and every endpoint fails the same way:
#   /api/branches  -> {"configured":false,"reason":"no-credentials"}
#   the four boards -> 500, "BLOBS_SITE_ID and BLOBS_TOKEN must be set together"
# Exactly one of the pair arriving is the tell.
#
# Start the preview with the `xcel-dashboard-hub` launch entry after filling
# this in. Nothing here is committed — .gitignore covers it.

# The Hub's site id. NOT a secret; it is in every deploy URL.
NETLIFY_SITE_ID=5e5209b8-6ed9-45b3-8881-780f5f2e7ffb

# A personal access token: Netlify → User settings → Applications →
# New access token. Only needs to read this site's deploys.
NETLIFY_API_TOKEN=

# Optional. Without it the rows still list, but the "On stage" and "Released"
# tags are missing and the section says the git facts are not configured.
# GitHub → Settings → Developer settings → fine-grained token, Contents: read
# on jillmoreno/xcel-ux-dashboard. (`gh auth token` prints one you already have.)
GITHUB_TOKEN=
